      payoff: "In 1986 around 35,000 come to Cross Maidan. Their money builds the plants that make Reliance one of India's largest companies.",
      meaning: "Dhirubhai treated the common man as his banker, and he was paid back in loyalty. India's habit of owning shares began here.",
